    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement on successful owner creation (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**New function** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n- Reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val`, and emits a single line on the logger named `NOTIFY` containing both the owner id and the `memberId`:\n  ```\n  NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n  ```\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `respond`, so it runs after `SaveOwner` (owner has its generated id) and `AssignOwnerMemberId` (memberId assigned), on the successful-create path only.\n\nThis follows the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern (dedicated named SLF4J logger) and satisfies the new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome`, which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts one line contains both the owner id and the fetched `memberId`.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass (the observed log confirms `NOTIFY - welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`).",
